{
  "text": "```verilog\nmodule areset_deassert_sync #(\n    parameter CHAINS = 2,\n    parameter RST_POL = 1'b1\n)(\n    input  clk,\n    input  async_rst_i,\n    output sync_rst_o\n);\n\n    localparam integer DEPTH = (CHAINS < 2) ? 2 : CHAINS;\n\n    reg [DEPTH-1:0] sync_reg;\n    reg             rst_active;\n\n    // Synchronize the reset signal\n    always @(posedge clk or posedge async_rst_i) begin\n        if (async_rst_i)\n            sync_reg <= {DEPTH{1'b1}};\n        else\n            sync_reg <= {sync_reg[DEPTH-2:0], 1'b1};\n    end\n\n    // Track whether reset is active (asserted)\n    // For active-high reset: reset is active when async_rst_i is high\n    // For active-low reset: reset is active when async_rst_i is low\n    wire rst_asserted = (RST_POL) ? async_rst_i : ~async_rst_i;\n\n    // The synchronized release signal: all bits are 1 means reset has been deasserted for DEPTH cycles\n    wire sync_released = &sync_reg;\n\n    // sync_rst_o is active (reset asserted) if:\n    // 1. The async reset is currently asserted (immediate assertion)\n    // 2. OR the synchronized release has not yet completed (still in release pipeline)\n    //\n    // For active-high reset (RST_POL=1):\n    //   sync_rst_o = 1 when reset is active\n    //   sync_rst_o = rst_asserted | ~sync_released\n    //\n    // For active-low reset (RST_POL=0):\n    //   sync_rst_o = 0 when reset is active (active-low means 0 is active)\n    //   sync_rst_o = ~rst_asserted & sync_released  ... wait, let me think again.\n    //\n    // Actually, let's define it more carefully:\n    // sync_rst_o should be in the \"reset active\" state when:\n    //   - async_rst_i is asserting reset (immediate)\n    //   - OR the deassertion has not yet been synchronized\n    //\n    // For RST_POL=1 (active-high): reset active = 1\n    //   sync_rst_o = rst_asserted | ~sync_released\n    //\n    // For RST_POL=0 (active-low): reset active = 0\n    //   sync_rst_o = ~rst_asserted & sync_released  ... no\n    //   When reset is active (async_rst_i=0 for active-low), sync_rst_o should be 0 (active)\n    //   When reset is released (async_rst_i=1 for active-low), sync_rst_o should go to 1 (inactive) after sync\n    //   So: sync_rst_o = rst_asserted ? 1'b0 : sync_released\n    //   Which is: sync_rst_o = ~rst_asserted & sync_released | rst_asserted & 1'b0\n    //   = ~rst_asserted & sync_released\n    //\n    // Let me unify:\n    // For RST_POL=1: sync_rst_o = rst_asserted | ~sync_released\n    // For RST_POL=0: sync_rst_o = ~rst_asserted & sync_released\n\n    assign sync_rst_o = (RST_POL) ? (rst_asserted | ~sync_released)\n                                  : (~rst_asserted & sync_released);\n\nendmodule\n```<|im_end|>",
